@startuml
title Logging Pipeline - Redis-like Server

' From a log call to the sinks, and the parts around it (SDD 5.1, 14.1;
' DX-OBS-6 to DX-OBS-11). Set-up is in main(); the level can change while the
' server runs. The watchdog and the crash report are separate paths.

start
:main() creates the logging guard
with --log-level and --log-file, and the four channels;

:init(): build the sinks
(stderr, and --log-file if it can be opened);
if (Log file cannot be opened?) then (yes)
  :Keep stderr only and log a warning
  "log file ... unavailable ...; stderr only";
endif
:Build an asynchronous logger:
a bounded queue (8192 lines) and one worker thread;
:Make the channels server, net, commands and persistence
as clones of that logger (same sinks, level and pattern);
if (Level name recognised?) then (no)
  :Fall back to info and log a warning
  "unknown log level ...; falling back to info";
endif
:install_crash_handler(--log-file);

note right
  Channels: server (startup, shutdown, signals, cron),
  net (connections), commands (requests and replies, trace),
  persistence (snapshot loads, SAVE, BGSAVE, AOF).
end note

partition "A log call, on any thread" {
  :logger_for(channel).<level>(...);
  if (Level at or above the channel's level?) then (no)
    :Dropped, nearly free;
  else (yes)
    :The arguments are formatted into the message;
    :Enqueue the line for the worker;
    if (Queue full?) then (yes)
      :The oldest queued line is dropped;
      note right
        The caller never blocks: the queue fills
        when the server is busiest.
      end note
    endif
    if (Level warning or above?) then (yes)
      :Flush at once;
    endif
  endif
}

partition "Logger worker thread" {
  :Take the next line off the queue;
  :Format "[time] [channel] [level] text";
  :Write to stderr;
  :Write to --log-file, if there is one;
}

partition "Level change while running" {
  :Client sends CONFIG SET loglevel <level>
  (only with --enable-config-set);
  if (Level name valid?) then (yes)
    :Set the level of the default logger
    and of every channel;
    :Log "Log level changed to <level> by CONFIG SET"
    (warning, server channel);
    :Reply +OK;
  else (no)
    :Reply "-ERR Invalid argument '<x>' for CONFIG SET 'loglevel'";
  endif
}

partition "Command watchdog thread (--watchdog-ms above 0)" {
  :Every 100 ms, read the running-command record;
  if (A command has run past --watchdog-ms?) then (yes)
    :Warn once per command, on the server channel:
    "Command '<name>' (<n> args) has been running for <ms> ms;
    no other command runs until it ends";
  endif
}

partition "Crash (POSIX only)" {
  :Fatal signal or uncaught exception;
  :Write "=== REDIS BUG REPORT START" ... "END" with write(2)
  to stderr and --log-file, not through the logger
  (signal, address, pid, running command, backtrace);
  :Run the signal's default action
  (core dump where enabled);
  note right
    The async queue dies with the process,
    so the report bypasses it.
  end note
}

partition "Exit" {
  :The guard's destructor calls shutdown():
  flush, join the worker (it writes what is still queued),
  then drop the loggers;
}

stop
@enduml
